## Facts
- `npm test` = `node scripts/run_node_runtime_gate.js` (build → typecheck → lint → runtime tests).
  Lint fails deterministically on `packages/framework/src/runtime/spots/spot-timer.ts:137:12`
  (`@typescript-eslint/strict-boolean-expressions`, nullable boolean in a condition), so the runtime
  test stage never runs in the standard gate (earlier campaign gates ran the runtime tests directly:
  1552 tests / 5 known items).
- Fix: make the condition explicit without changing behaviour (e.g. `=== true` / `?? false` matching
  the surrounding code's convention; read the field's type and the existing style in that file).

## What to do
1. Apply the one-line lint fix; `npm run lint` must be fully green.
2. Run the full standard gate `npm test` once and record the runtime test counts (pass/fail/skip) and
   every failure with `file:line`, classified (A) DONTWAIT/backpressure, (B) terminal/error,
   (C) known pre-existing with prior evidence `file:line`, (D) environment, (E) binding-port.
   Known earlier C items: ZoneWorld dist-not-built ×3 (dist now exists — expect them green).
3. Re-run any failing test file once for determinism.

